<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Werner I of Strasbourg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1028</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Werner of Habsburg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Werner I was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of Strasbourg from 1001 to 1028 and a member of the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> family. A loyal supporter of Emperor Henry II, he began the Romanesque cathedral of Strasbourg in 1015. Tradition credits him, with his relative Count Radbot, with building <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-castle">Habsburg Castle</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aargau">Aargau</a> around 1020 to 1030, the castle that gave the dynasty its name. He died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> while on an imperial embassy.</p></div>
